# AI context and style guide for chFPGA documentation

Style preferences, conventions, and context for AI-assisted documentation work on the chFPGA project.

Rules are split by topic:

- **RST and documentation**: .cursor/rules/rst_rules.mdc (applies to *.rst)
  - Image organization, RST file structure and formatting, common issues and fixes, file locations, module documentation patterns, memory map reference

- **SVG block diagrams**: .cursor/rules/svg_rules.mdc (applies to *.svg)
  - SVG block diagram style

- **VHDL** (including comment extraction for Sphinx): .cursor/rules/vhdl_rules.mdc (always applied)
  - VHDL coding style (port maps, VHDL2008, AXI naming, etc.)
  - VHDL comment extraction (vhdl_sphinx_domain), memory map table format in VHDL comments

- **XDC constraints**: .cursor/rules/xdc_rules.mdc (applies to *.xdc)
  - Cell names, LVDS differential pairs

- **General principles for .rst**: .cursor/rules/principles.mdc (applies to *.rst)

- **Git commit style**: .cursor/rules/git_rules.mdc (always applied)

See those files for the full rule text.
